.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SMIME_WRITE_ASN1 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SMIME_write_ASN1_ex ,
.Nm SMIME_write_ASN1
.Nd convert structure to S/MIME format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft int
.Fo SMIME_write_ASN1_ex
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE *val"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "int ctype_nid"
.Fa "int econt_nid"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_ALGOR) *mdalgs"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SMIME_write_ASN1
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE *val"
.Fa "BIO *data"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fa "int ctype_nid"
.Fa "int econt_nid"
.Fa "STACK_OF(X509_ALGOR) *mdalgs"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SMIME_write_ASN1_ex
adds the appropriate MIME headers to an object structure to produce an
S/MIME message.
.Pp
.Fa out
is the BIO to write the data to.
.Em value
is the appropriate ASN1_VALUE structure (either CMS_ContentInfo or
PKCS7). If streaming is enabled then the content must be supplied via
.Fa data .
.Fa flags
is an optional set of flags.
.Fa ctype_nid
is the NID of the content type,
.Fa econt_nid
is the NID of the embedded content type and
.Fa mdalgs
is a list of signed data digestAlgorithms.
Valid values that can be used by the ASN.1 structure
.Fa it
are ASN1_ITEM_rptr(PKCS7) or ASN1_ITEM_rptr(CMS_ContentInfo).
The library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
.Sh NOTES
The higher level functions
.Xr SMIME_write_CMS 3
and
.Xr SMIME_write_PKCS7 3
should be used instead of
.Fn SMIME_write_ASN1 .
.Pp
The following flags can be passed in the
.Fa flags
parameter.
.Pp
If
.Sy CMS_DETACHED
is set then cleartext signing will be used, this option only makes sense
for SignedData where
.Sy CMS_DETACHED
is also set when the
.Xr sign 3
method is called.
.Pp
If the
.Sy CMS_TEXT
flag is set MIME headers for type
.Sy text/plain
are added to the content, this only makes sense if
.Sy CMS_DETACHED
is also set.
.Pp
If the
.Sy CMS_STREAM
flag is set streaming is performed.
This flag should only be set if
.Sy CMS_STREAM
was also set in the previous call to a CMS_ContentInfo or PKCS7 creation
function.
.Pp
If cleartext signing is being used and
.Sy CMS_STREAM
not set then the data must be read twice: once to compute the signature
in sign method and once to output the S/MIME message.
.Pp
If streaming is performed the content is output in BER format using
indefinite length constructed encoding except in the case of signed data
with detached content where the content is absent and DER format is
used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SMIME_write_ASN1_ex
and
.Fn SMIME_write_ASN1
return 1 for success or 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr SMIME_write_CMS 3 ,
.Xr SMIME_write_PKCS7 3
